---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import '../styles/about.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Background, education, and the work I do: a WGU B.S. in AI Engineering (expected September 2027), 11 published Rust crates, synthetic-factory, and merged upstream PRs.">
  <section class="page-intro" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 id="about-title">About me.</h1>
    <p>I'm {site.fullName}. I live in San Marcos, Texas, and I'm open to relocating.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="about-profile" aria-label="Professional background">
    <figure><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/raul-cardenas-montoya-256.webp 256w, /assets/raul-cardenas-montoya-512.webp 512w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 90vw, 380px" /><img src="/assets/raul-cardenas-montoya-512.jpg" srcset="/assets/raul-cardenas-montoya-256.jpg 256w, /assets/raul-cardenas-montoya-512.jpg 512w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 90vw, 380px" width="512" height="512" alt="Raul Cardenas Montoya" loading="eager" /></picture><figcaption>Raul Cardenas Montoya, San Marcos, TX.</figcaption></figure>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Most of what I build is infrastructure for agentic systems, synthetic data, and model evaluation. synthetic-factory is a synthetic-data platform where unknown provenance resolves to blocked and every record replays from its pack, seed, and actions. I've published 60 datasets from it on Hugging Face. agoge-forger is a local-first LoRA/QLoRA post-training harness with immutable manifests, split-integrity checks, and leakage detection.</p>
      <p>I've published 11 Rust crates on crates.io, including neuromod (2,000+ downloads) and nir-rs (1,000+). The spiking-network demo on the homepage runs on four of them. Upstream, I implemented the xAI/Grok provider in agent-afk, and I added Linux support and Devin usage tracking to UsagePal. Both sets of PRs are merged.</p>
      <p>I'm working toward a B.S. in Artificial Intelligence Engineering at Western Governors University, expected September 2027. Before that I took Electrical Engineering coursework at Texas State University and Computer Science coursework at Concordia Texas University and Austin Community College.</p>
      <p>I work in Rust, Python, Julia, and CUDA C/C++, mostly on Fedora Linux. The fastest way to reach me is <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, and my <a href={site.resumePath}>résumé is a PDF</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
